{
  "_readme": [
    "Copy this to my_wardrobe.json and replace it with your actual clothes.",
    "Run:  PUDDLE_WARDROBE=my_wardrobe.json python3 scripts/wardrobe_check.py",
    "",
    "You write title, price and wears. Category, formality, warmth, kind and",
    "rain are inferred from the words in the title. State any of them",
    "explicitly to override the guess.",
    "",
    "wears  = roughly how many times you have worn it. It does not need to be",
    "         exact; it is what tells the engine which occasions your life",
    "         actually consists of. Things you never wear should be 0 or 1.",
    "",
    "purchases = what you have BOUGHT, including things you sent back. This is",
    "         where the duck's best lines come from, so it matters more than",
    "         the closet. 'hour' is the hour of day you bought it (0-23) and",
    "         'returned' is whether you sent it back."
